      "rev_n_15_846b72_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_15_846b72_1",
        "node_id": "n_15_846b72",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of checking reachability from each room individually can miss cycles that involve multiple rooms. Instead, we should consider the overall structure of the conveyor belts and their interactions. The key insight is that a room is returnable if and only if it's part of a strongly connected component (SCC) in the graph formed by the conveyor belts, where each SCC represents a cycle or a set of rooms that can reach each other. This allows us to efficiently identify all returnable rooms in a single pass through the graph.",
